    {
      "diff": "@@ -28,16 +28,15 @@ wsbuglink:18734[].\n \n The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-* wssalink:2023-08[]\n-ISO 15765 and ISO 10681 dissector crash.\n-wsbuglink:18839[].\n+// * wssalink:2023-09[]\n+// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n+// wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n // cveidlink:2023-xxxx[].\n // Fixed in master: b4c784805c\n // Fixed in release-4.0: 4ec72ec3a1\n // Fixed in release-3.6: 51e23ea7fd\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n-// CWE-120\n-// * ISO15765 and ISO10681 dissectors corrupt memory and Wireshark may crash. wsbuglink:18839[].\n+// CWE-xxx\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -46,30 +45,6 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark insists on subscribing to two dozen streaming services but only watches three.\n \n-* UTF-8 characters end up escaped in PSML output. wsbuglink:10445[].\n-* Export filtered displayed packets won't save IP fragments of SCTP fragments needed to reassemble a displayed frame. wsbuglink:12597[].\n-* DICOM dissection in reassembled PDV goes wrong. wsbuglink:13388[].\n-* \"Export Objects - IMF\" produces incorrect file, TCP reassembly fails with retransmissions that have additional data. wsbuglink:13523[].\n-* The intelligent scroll bar or minimap is not predictable on locating and scrolling. wsbuglink:13989[].\n-* If you mark (or unmark) the currently-selected frame, the packet details still say it's not marked (or it is marked) wsbuglink:14330[].\n-* An out-of-order packet incorrectly detected as retransmission breaks desegmentation of TCP stream. wsbuglink:15993[].\n-* Sorting Packet Loss Column is not sorting correct. wsbuglink:16785[].\n-* Some HTTPS packets cannot be decrypted. wsbuglink:17406[].\n-* SIP TCP decoding regression from Wireshark 1.99.0 to 3.6.8. wsbuglink:18411[].\n-* Frame comments not preserved when using filter to write new pcap from tshark. wsbuglink:18693[].\n-* ChmodBPF not working on macOS Ventura 13.1. wsbuglink:18734[].\n-* Wireshark GUI and window manager stuck after setting display filter. wsbuglink:18809[].\n-* Dissector bug, protocol H.261. wsbuglink:18812[].\n-* File extension heuristics are case-sensitive. wsbuglink:18821[].\n-* Symbolic links to packages in macOS dmg can't be double-clicked to install on macOS 13.2. wsbuglink:18830[].\n-* Potential memory leak in tshark.c. wsbuglink:18837[].\n-* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-02-05-7303.pcap. wsbuglink:18842[].\n-* f5fileinfo: Hardware platforms missing descriptions. wsbuglink:18848[].\n-* The lines in the intelligent scrollbar are off by one. wsbuglink:18850[].\n-* Wireshark crashes on invalid UDS packet in Lua context. wsbuglink:18865[].\n-* TECMP dissector shows the wrong Voltage in Vendor Data. wsbuglink:18871[].\n-* UDS: Names of RDTCI subfunctions 0x0b ... 0x0e are not correct. wsbuglink:18873[].\n-\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new or updated features in this release.\n@@ -94,36 +69,6 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.0.4.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-ASTERIX\n-BGP\n-DHCP\n-ERF\n-F5 Ethernet trailer\n-GMR-1 RR\n-Gryphon\n-GSM SMS\n-H.261\n-H.450\n-ISO 10681\n-ISO 15765\n-MIPv6\n-NAS-5gs\n-NR RRC\n-NS Trace\n-OptoMMP\n-PDCP-LTE\n-PDCP-NR\n-QSIG\n-ROHC\n-RSVP\n-RTCP\n-SCTP\n-SIP\n-TCP\n-TECMP\n-TWAMP\n-UDS\n-UMTS RLC\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
